<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a>–<a href="/years/1835">1835</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Francis I of Austria, Franz II · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">House of Habsburg-Lorraine</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, from 1792 to 1806, and as Francis I the first Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, from 1804 to 1835. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany">Leopold II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-luisa-duchess-of-lucca">Maria Luisa of Spain</a>, he succeeded his father during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a> and led Austria against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> through a series of defeats. After Napoleon created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> he abdicated as Holy Roman Emperor in 1806, which in effect dissolved the empire, and after the defeat of the Fifth Coalition he had to marry his daughter Marie Louise to Napoleon. From 1813 he helped defeat Napoleon, and he was the first president of the German Confederation from 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Francis II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="330" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich von Amerling · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francis_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor_by_Friedrich_von_Amerling_(4x5_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
